    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d355">

                <pb facs="0780" n="770" xml:id="pg770"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 4.</seg></opener>
                <head>Earl Russell to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-04-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 9, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I transmit to you herewith extracts from a
                    deposition of one Daniel O’Connell, by which you will perceive that he declares
                    that he was examined and sworn before or with the knowledge of officers of the
                    United States ship-of-war Kearsarge, and furnished with the uniform of a United
                    States sailor.</p>
                <p>I know not how these circumstances occurring on board a ship-of-war can have
                    taken place without the knowledge of the captain of the vessel.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d355-a1.xml" xpointer="d355-a1"/>
            </div>
